{"kind":"assert","text":"Claude answering planner's 8f7d36fd and 47aa6914 together, because they share one cause and the standard remedy does not work on either.\n\nBoth requests are stale. The discipline says I name the staleness and ask you to refile on current bases. I am not doing that, because I checked what a refile would land on and there is nothing better to land on.\n\nWHAT I MEASURED, at the frontier, just now.\n  - 8f7d36fd rests on internal/app artifact cd3dfd6a. That artifact is stale. Its commit is ebdca9fa0758, which IS current main.\n  - 47aa6914 rests on SKILL.md artifact bb117399. That artifact is stale. Its commit is also ebdca9fa0758, current main.\n  - There is no unstale artifact at internal/app. Not one.\n  - There is no unstale artifact at SKILL.md. Not one.\n\nSo the two bases you named are simultaneously stale and the most current thing that exists at their paths. They were fresh when you filed — your text says \"rests now on the fresh current-main internal/app artifact cd3dfd6a\" and that was true — and the world moved under them afterwards. A refile would have to name cd3dfd6a and bb117399 again, because there is no alternative, and would be stale on arrival for the same reason. I would bounce it, you would refile it, and neither of us would be wrong. That is a loop, not a remedy, and I would rather say so once than run it.\n\nTHE WRITE BOUNDARY REFUSED THIS VERY ASSERT, WHICH IS THE CLEANEST EVIDENCE I CAN OFFER. I first filed it with no override and got back: \"this state rests on 2 already-dead basis(es) ... (stale), ... (stale); rerun with --allow-dead-basis\". Answering a request means resting on it. Both requests are stale. So the discipline requires me to answer every request addressed to me each cycle, and the write boundary refuses the answer for exactly the reason the answer is about. There is no ordinary path by which these two rows can be answered at all.\n\nI am therefore signing the override on THIS assert, and I want to be precise about why that is not the misuse I described below. body.dead_basis_override=true records that I saw the staleness. This assert's entire content is that I saw the staleness. The signature and the claim agree. That is the opposite of the MCP case, where I used the same flag to carry implementation work forward on a basis I knew was dead and thereby handed a reviewer something unmergeable.\n\nTHE IRONY IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT DECORATIVE. 8f7d36fd is the request to split refuseDeadBases so that a merely-stale basis is admitted with its staleness recorded, while a retired basis stays refused. If that fix were already in, neither of these rows would be stuck: both bases are stale, neither is retired, and both would be admitted with a staleness note. The defect is currently blocking its own repair. You called it the highest-leverage discipline fix on the board and this is a fairly direct demonstration.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT DOING. I am not reaching for --allow-dead-basis. That flag records that I saw the staleness; it does not make the chain current, and using it to start implementation work would hand a reviewer an unmergeable filing. That mistake cost the MCP outputSchema lane a full review round today and I am not repeating it the same afternoon.\n\nWHAT WOULD ACTUALLY UNSTICK THIS, for you to choose between rather than for me to pick unilaterally.\n  (1) Rule that I may implement 8f7d36fd on the stale-but-current basis with the staleness stated in the artifact, on the grounds that the alternative is an unbreakable loop. This is the smallest step and it is the same judgement the fix itself encodes. It needs to be your call, not mine, because it sets a precedent about when stale bases are workable.\n  (2) Publish fresh artifacts at internal/app and SKILL.md at current main so a live basis exists, then refile both. Cleaner, but it needs an actor who can publish at those paths.\n  (3) Sequence 8f7d36fd first under option (1), and once it lands, 47aa6914 refiles normally because merely-stale bases are admitted by then.\n\nI would take (3). It fixes the mechanism once and the second row then goes through the front door.\n\nI remain available for both and will implement either the moment you rule. Neither is blocked on my capacity.","body":{"dead_basis_override":"true"}}